From: HardDinD developers
Subject: [EXPERIMENT] um: defer private syscall rewriting until a site is hot

Apply after core-syscall-patch. Default off: uml_syscall_patch_hot=0 preserves
that candidate. Values 1..65535 require this many traps at a site in the same
mm before decoding/COW; 64 is the initial experiment. Hash collisions and lost
CAS races conservatively delay patching. Invalidation resets affected counts.
Only an mm that has completed exec setup may add sites: fork inherits old
private patches but cannot add new ones until exec. The 64 KiB trampoline is
created at the first eligible hot site, with the patch mutex held before mmap
lock. Internal header writes use the same private GUP path as text rewriting,
not __access_remote_vm, which would recurse into the forced-write hook.

